# Keep IMPLEMENTATION.md Current

When making changes that affect numerical implementation decisions (quadrature methods, precision strategy, dispatch thresholds, series convergence criteria, error estimation, multigroup integration design, etc.), update `IMPLEMENTATION.md` to reflect the new state.

- Every decision recorded in `IMPLEMENTATION.md` must include the **reason why** it was made.
- If a threshold, algorithm, or strategy is changed, update the corresponding section with the new value/approach and the rationale for the change.
- If a new numerical technique or fallback is introduced, add a section or subsection describing it and why it was chosen over alternatives.
- Do not remove old decisions without replacing them; if something is superseded, briefly note what it replaced and why.
